reply:
Here is an interactive vocabulary study surface designed using the components from the catalog. 

This UI is split into two sections using a multi-column layout (`columns`):
1. **Left Panel**: Contains the header info, a highly visual circular progress indicator (`progress_ring`) showing that 7 out of 10 cards have been reviewed, and a motivational status update callout (`text_callout`).
2. **Right Panel**: Houses a responsive interactive flashcard deck (`flashcard_deck`) containing exactly 10 high-yield SAT/GRE vocabulary words with flip triggers, definitions, and contextual example sentences.

### A2UI Payload

First, we signal the client to create the interactive surface:

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9.1",
  "createSurface": {
    "surfaceId": "vocab-study-deck",
    "catalogId": "https://a2uicatalog.ai/catalog/c-learning.json"
  }
}
</a2ui-json>

Next, we render the components onto our newly created surface:

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9.1",
  "updateComponents": {
    "surfaceId": "vocab-study-deck",
    "components": [
      {
        "id": "root",
        "component": "columns",
        "cols": 2,
        "gap": "2.5rem",
        "align": "top",
        "items": [
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "header",
                "component": "page_header",
                "title": "# Advanced Vocabulary Builder",
                "subtitle": "Master high-frequency academic vocabulary with interactive flashcards. Click on any card in the deck to flip and reveal its definition and usage.",
                "icon": "📚",
                "accent": "#4f46e5"
              },
              {
                "id": "progress",
                "component": "progress_ring",
                "value": "70",
                "size": "140",
                "stroke_width": "10",
                "color": "#4f46e5",
                "label": "Review Progress",
                "show_value": "true",
                "unit": "%"
              },
              {
                "id": "motivation-banner",
                "component": "text_callout",
                "variant": "success",
                "title": "Daily Goal: 70% Completed",
                "description": "Awesome job! You have successfully reviewed 7 out of 10 vocabulary cards. Only 3 more left to secure your streak for today!"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "vocabulary-deck",
                "component": "flashcard_deck",
                "accent": "#4f46e5",
                "label_front": "TERM",
                "label_back": "DEFINITION & EXAMPLE",
                "cards": [
                  {
                    "front": "Anachronism",
                    "back": "Something located as most associated with a time other than that in which it exists.\n\n*Example*: \"The digital watch worn by the actor in the medieval drama was a glaring anachronism.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Ephemeral",
                    "back": "Lasting for a very short time; transient or fleeting.\n\n*Example*: \"The vibrant colors of the sunset were beautiful but ephemeral.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Capricious",
                    "back": "Given to sudden and unaccountable changes of mood or behavior.\n\n*Example*: \"With the region's capricious weather, we could experience rain, snow, and sunshine all in one afternoon.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Loquacious",
                    "back": "Tending to talk a great deal; extremely talkative.\n\n*Example*: \"The normally loquacious host was uncharacteristically quiet during the debate.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Taciturn",
                    "back": "Reserved or uncommunicative in speech; saying little.\n\n*Example*: \"A taciturn man by nature, he preferred observing the room rather than participating in gossip.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Pernicious",
                    "back": "Having a harmful effect, especially in a gradual or subtle way.\n\n*Example*: \"The pernicious rumors quietly eroded the team's trust in their leadership.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Assiduous",
                    "back": "Showing great care, attention, and effort; highly diligent.\n\n*Example*: \"Through assiduous research, the scientists finally identified the source of the outbreak.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Obsequious",
                    "back": "Obedient or attentive to an excessive, fawning, or servile degree.\n\n*Example*: \"The manager was surrounded by obsequious assistants who agreed with his every word.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Pragmatic",
                    "back": "Dealing with things sensibly and realistically based on practical rather than theoretical considerations.\n\n*Example*: \"Rather than dreaming of perfect scenarios, they took a pragmatic approach to solve the budget deficit.\""
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Cacophony",
                    "back": "A harsh, discordant mixture of sounds.\n\n*Example*: \"A loud cacophony of car horns, construction drills, and shouting pedestrians filled the morning air.\""
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
</a2ui-json>
